==Battleground==
*1 [[Urs & Fenrir (Enemy)|Urs & Fenrir]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*8 [[Croconator]]s spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
*3 [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]] spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*400 [[Croconator]]s spawn, delay 8~12 seconds<sup>240f~360f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The use of units with more than 500 range is highly recommended. Using dual Erasers and [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] is a great help.

[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]] can be used to stall the Croconators, which will allow you to stack LD units such as [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]] and [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]]. Because of Urs' low HP combined with their high knockback count, Urs will constantly be knocked back, preventing them from securing much damage on the base.

Alternatively, Urs can be stalled at the base by spamming [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]] and Green Shell until Rain D appears. Lure Rain D to the base and rush him with [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. Afterwards, [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] along with other units such as [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] will help you rush Urs down. Bring something to deal with the second Rain D, such as [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]]. In the event that Urs survives, it is likely they can be chipped down by Jelly Dumpling due to their rather low base HP.

On 2 or 3* difficulty, Urs can be lured to the base while the Croconators are again stalled by Green Shell. When Urs is close enough, you can use Manic Lion Cat to get rid of the Croconators before rushing them down by sending out [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] followed by [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]] and Awakened Bahamut Cat.

